    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. **frai-core/src/eval/index.js** - Core threshold logic\n- Updated `generateReport` to accept an optional `thresholds` object\n- Calculates which thresholds pass/fail based on metric scores\n- Adds `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array) fields to reports when thresholds are provided\n- Thresholds with no score (metric not found) automatically fail\n\n### 2. **frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js** - Markdown reporting\n- Added \"Thresholds\" section to markdown reports showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold\n- Displays metric ID, status, minimum required score, and actual score\n\n### 3. **frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js** - Tests\n- Added 3 comprehensive tests:\n  - Passing thresholds\n  - Failing thresholds\n  - Null scores (missing metrics)\n\n### 4. **frai-cli/src/index.ts** - CLI implementation\n- Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (repeatable)\n- `parseThresholds()` function validates format: `<metric>=<number>`\n- `validateMetricIds()` checks against valid metrics: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`\n- **Exit codes:**\n  - Exit 0: All thresholds pass (or no thresholds)\n  - Exit 1: Any threshold fails\n  - Exit 2: Malformed threshold or unknown metric ID (lists valid IDs)\n- Report is always written, even when thresholds fail\n\n### 5. **README.md** - Documentation\n- Added documentation for the `--threshold` option with examples\n\n## Key Features\n\u2705 Works with custom metrics (SDK users can pass any metric IDs via `generateReport`)\n\u2705 Backward compatible (no `--threshold` = original behavior)\n\u2705 Validates threshold format and values (0-1 range)\n\u2705 Reports include threshold results (JSON and Markdown formats)\n\u2705 Can specify multiple thresholds: `frai eval --outputs file.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`",
